WEBVTT

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:27.568
The Jungle Book by Rudyard Kipling Copyright Black Cat Publishing Chapter 1 Moegley's Family One evening in the hills of South India, Father Wolf wakes up.

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:32.436
Mother Wolf is near him with four little cubs.

00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:35.118
It's time to look for food.

00:00:35.177 --> 00:00:37.530
Says Father Wolf.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.152
He gets up and leaves the cave.

00:00:41.212 --> 00:00:44.824
There is a big moon in the sky.

00:00:44.884 --> 00:00:46.496
Hello.

00:00:46.556 --> 00:00:48.448
Says a voice.

00:00:48.508 --> 00:00:51.540
It is the Jackal tobacco.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.285
He eats everything, even old clothes from the villages.

00:00:57.345 --> 00:01:01.960
The wolves do not like him and are afraid of him.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.522
What do you want, Tabakwein?

00:01:04.582 --> 00:01:06.724
asks Father Wolf.

00:01:06.784 --> 00:01:12.328
The tiger, Sheer Khan, is coming here to look for food.

00:01:12.388 --> 00:01:14.100
Says Tabakwein.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.310
What?

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.844
Says Father Wolf surprised.

00:01:18.904 --> 00:01:20.956
He can't do that.

00:01:21.016 --> 00:01:25.666
He must tell us first because that's the law of the jungle.

00:01:25.726 --> 00:01:31.385
Sheer Khan has a bad leg and he can't run fast.

00:01:31.445 --> 00:01:33.816
Says Mother Wolf.

00:01:33.876 --> 00:01:40.879
He only kills bulls and the people of the village are angry with him.

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:43.651
That's why he's coming here.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.722
He wants to start hunting in a new place.

00:01:47.782 --> 00:01:49.323
Listen.

00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:51.444
Says Tabakui.

00:01:51.504 --> 00:01:54.658
You can hear him in the woods.

00:01:54.718 --> 00:02:01.234
Father Wolf listens and says, What a stupid animal.

00:02:01.294 --> 00:02:08.236
He's making a lot of noise, and all the animals are going to run away and hide.

00:02:08.296 --> 00:02:11.467
How can I look for food now?

00:02:11.526 --> 00:02:15.738
Shh, says Mother Wolf.

00:02:15.797 --> 00:02:19.469
It's the noise of a man.

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:22.020
A man?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.466
Cries Father Wolf.

00:02:24.526 --> 00:02:38.950
The law of the jungle says that animals must not eat man because then a lot of men with guns come to the jungle and all of the animals are in danger.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.912
Listen, says Mother Wolf.

00:02:42.972 --> 00:02:46.934
Something's coming to the cave.

00:02:46.994 --> 00:02:52.303
Father Wolf sees a baby standing under a tree.

00:02:52.363 --> 00:02:57.290
The baby looks at Father Wolf and laughs.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:00.321
Is that a man cub?

00:03:00.381 --> 00:03:03.012
asks Mother Wolf.

00:03:03.072 --> 00:03:05.283
Bring it here.

00:03:05.343 --> 00:03:08.424
I want to look at it.

00:03:08.484 --> 00:03:13.466
The baby is small and has no clothes.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:18.327
Father Wolf gently carries it to Mother Wolf.

00:03:18.387 --> 00:03:22.694
It starts drinking her milk with the other cubs.

00:03:22.754 --> 00:03:30.854
Mother Wolf is happy and says, Look, he's drinking my milk with the cubs.

00:03:30.914 --> 00:03:33.426
He's not afraid.

00:03:33.486 --> 00:03:41.550
It is suddenly dark in the cave because Sheer Khan puts his big head inside.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.612
We're pleased to see you, Sheer Khan.

00:03:45.672 --> 00:03:50.984
Says Father Wolf, but his eyes are angry.

00:03:51.044 --> 00:03:52.847
I know.

00:03:52.906 --> 00:03:55.970
There's a man cub here.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.792
Says Sheer Khan.

00:03:58.852 --> 00:04:01.112
It's mine.

00:04:01.172 --> 00:04:04.675
You must give it to me.

00:04:04.735 --> 00:04:10.979
Sheer Khan's very big, so he can't come into the cave.

00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:13.420
Thinks Father Wolf.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.402
The man cub is ours.

00:04:16.462 --> 00:04:18.498
Says Father Wolf.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:23.525
The leader of the pack's going to decide what to do with the cub.

00:04:23.585 --> 00:04:27.156
We listen to him, and not to a tiger.

00:04:27.216 --> 00:04:31.308
The man cub is mine.

00:04:31.368 --> 00:04:34.329
Cry's sheer calm angrily.

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:37.270
He starts roaring.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.401
No!

00:04:39.461 --> 00:04:41.856
Cry's mother wolf.

00:04:41.915 --> 00:04:46.822
The man cub is mine, and you can't kill him.

00:04:46.881 --> 00:04:48.953
He's going to live with us.

00:04:49.013 --> 00:04:50.644
He's my son.

00:04:50.704 --> 00:04:53.056
Now go away!

00:04:53.116 --> 00:04:59.770
Sheer Khan walks around the cave slowly and looks at the man cub.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.590
No.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:07.754
I'm Sheer Khan, and the cub is mine.

00:05:07.814 --> 00:05:11.618
You're wrong, says Mother Wolf.

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:14.190
The man cub is ours.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.162
He's going to live with us.

00:05:16.222 --> 00:05:18.414
He's my son.

00:05:18.474 --> 00:05:21.626
Now go away, Sheer Khan.

00:05:21.686 --> 00:05:28.862
Father Wolf is surprised, but he knows Mother Wolf is brave and strong.

00:05:28.922 --> 00:05:31.414
Sheer Khan goes away.

00:05:31.474 --> 00:05:36.138
He knows he cannot fight Mother Wolf in the cave.

00:05:36.198 --> 00:05:40.841
One day, I'm going to have that cub.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.765
He cries.

00:05:42.825 --> 00:05:50.650
After Sheer Khan leaves, Father Wolf says, Do you really want to keep him?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:55.592
Yes, I do, says Mother Wolf.

00:05:55.652 --> 00:06:00.793
He isn't afraid of us, and he's happy here.

00:06:00.853 --> 00:06:05.284
I want to call him Mowgli the Frog.

00:06:05.344 --> 00:06:06.744
Mowgli?

00:06:06.804 --> 00:06:08.935
Says Father Wolf.

00:06:08.995 --> 00:06:12.638
Yes, I like the name Mowgli.

00:06:12.698 --> 00:06:16.212
We must show Mowgli to the pack.

00:06:16.272 --> 00:06:28.005
The law of the jungle says that the pack must see all of the wolf cubs when they can walk and look at them carefully.

00:06:28.065 --> 00:06:32.677
Listening activity.

00:06:32.736 --> 00:06:36.848
My name is Baloo.

00:06:36.907 --> 00:06:39.339
I'm a big bear.

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:45.024
and I live in the jungle with baguera and the wounds.

00:06:45.084 --> 00:06:51.067
I teach the cubs in the wolf pack about the lore of the jungle.

00:06:51.127 --> 00:06:55.110
I know all the animals in the jungle.

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:59.902
I am their friend, and I can speak their language.

00:06:59.962 --> 00:07:02.574
They know I don't hunt.

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:08.488
I only eat nuts and honey.

00:07:08.548 --> 00:07:11.740
I'm Bagheera.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.463
I'm a black panther.

00:07:14.522 --> 00:07:17.194
I'm very strong.

00:07:17.254 --> 00:07:22.328
All the other animals say, I'm clever.

00:07:22.388 --> 00:07:28.392
They often ask me about things and ask me to help them.

00:07:28.452 --> 00:07:33.666
I'm going to help Baloo teach Mowgli, the man cub.

00:07:33.725 --> 00:07:38.957
I know about men, and I know they are clever too.

00:07:39.017 --> 00:07:45.226
I hope I can teach him everything he needs to know to live in the jungle.

00:07:45.286 --> 00:07:50.336
It's a difficult place to live.

00:07:50.396 --> 00:07:54.088
Chapter 2.

00:07:54.148 --> 00:08:05.990
Council Rock When the four wolf cubs can walk, father wolf takes them and moogly to council rock.

00:08:06.049 --> 00:08:08.840
Mother wolf goes to.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:17.774
Hundreds of wolves in the wolf pack meet at council rock once a month when the moon is full.

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:24.768
Akela is the leader of the pack and he sits on a big rock.

00:08:24.828 --> 00:08:29.992
He is a grey wolf and he is very brave.

00:08:30.052 --> 00:08:39.044
Each new wolf cub stands in front of him and he says, Look carefully, wolves!

00:08:39.104 --> 00:08:41.574
Look carefully!

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:49.246
At last, Father Wolf pushes Mowgli in front of Akhala and the other wolves.

00:08:49.306 --> 00:08:52.677
This is Mowgli, the frog.

00:08:52.737 --> 00:08:55.058
Says Father Wolf.

00:08:55.118 --> 00:08:57.938
Mowgli just laughs.

00:08:57.998 --> 00:09:04.052
Suddenly, the wolves hear Sheer Khan's voice behind the trees.

00:09:04.112 --> 00:09:07.655
The man cub is mine.

00:09:07.715 --> 00:09:09.696
Give him to me."

00:09:09.756 --> 00:09:11.638
He cries.

00:09:11.698 --> 00:09:17.591
Akela does not move, but says, Look carefully.

00:09:17.651 --> 00:09:21.213
Who speaks for this man cub?

00:09:21.273 --> 00:09:28.536
Two voices must speak for him, but not his father and mother.

00:09:28.596 --> 00:09:34.959
A big, sleepy, brown bear appears in front of Akhala.

00:09:35.019 --> 00:09:36.650
Baloo!

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:39.772
says Akhala, surprised.

00:09:39.832 --> 00:09:48.158
Baloo teaches the law of the jungle to the wolf cubs, and he speaks at the meetings of the council.

00:09:48.219 --> 00:09:53.252
Everyone likes him because he eats only nuts and honey.

00:09:53.312 --> 00:09:55.394
He doesn't hunt.

00:09:55.454 --> 00:10:02.188
I can speak for the man cub, says Balu with his low voice.

00:10:02.248 --> 00:10:06.950
I can teach him to run with the pack.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.220
Very well.

00:10:09.281 --> 00:10:11.442
Says Akela.

00:10:11.502 --> 00:10:17.454
Another animal silently jumps down into the circle of wolves.

00:10:17.514 --> 00:10:20.544
It is Bagira the Panther.

00:10:20.604 --> 00:10:24.544
He is black, brave and strong.

00:10:24.604 --> 00:10:27.894
He is also very clever.

00:10:27.954 --> 00:10:31.944
Akhala, can I speak?

00:10:32.004 --> 00:10:34.635
asks Bagheera softly.

00:10:34.695 --> 00:10:36.815
Yes, you can.

00:10:36.875 --> 00:10:38.455
Says Akhala.

00:10:38.515 --> 00:10:46.887
The law of the jungle says it's possible to buy the life of a cub.

00:10:46.947 --> 00:10:48.907
Says Bagheera.

00:10:48.967 --> 00:10:55.349
It's bad to kill a man cub because he can't hurt you.

00:10:55.409 --> 00:11:02.102
Let him live, and I can give you a fat bull to eat.

00:11:02.162 --> 00:11:05.062
Good, good.

00:11:05.123 --> 00:11:07.513
Say the young wolves.

00:11:07.573 --> 00:11:12.994
They are always hungry and want to eat the fat bull.

00:11:13.055 --> 00:11:15.565
Let him live.

00:11:15.625 --> 00:11:17.656
Very well.

00:11:17.716 --> 00:11:20.036
Says Akela.

00:11:20.096 --> 00:11:23.538
Look carefully, wolves.

00:11:23.598 --> 00:11:26.763
Look carefully.

00:11:26.823 --> 00:11:32.762
The wolves walk near Mowgli and look at him carefully.

00:11:32.822 --> 00:11:44.288
Then they go away and only Akela, Balu, Beguira and Mowgli's wolf family are at the council.

00:11:44.348 --> 00:11:49.142
They can hear sheer calm roaring in the night.

00:11:49.202 --> 00:11:53.614
Men and their cubs are clever.

00:11:53.674 --> 00:11:55.569
Says Akela.

00:11:55.629 --> 00:11:59.994
One day, this man cub can help us.

00:12:00.055 --> 00:12:07.168
Now, take him away and teach him everything he must know.

00:12:07.228 --> 00:12:18.897
Thanks to Baloo's good words and Beguira's fat bull, Mowgli now belongs to the Cioni wolf pack.

00:12:18.958 --> 00:12:28.306
He grows up in the wolf family and he learns the songs of the birds and the sounds of the animals in the jungle.

00:12:28.366 --> 00:12:33.067
Baloo and Beguira are very good teachers.

00:12:33.127 --> 00:12:40.320
He learns to climb trees, swim in the river and hunt for his food.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:46.144
He is a happy boy.

00:12:46.204 --> 00:12:52.430
lessons with Baloo.

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:57.212
Mowgli is now around 10 years old.

00:12:57.272 --> 00:13:02.654
Baloo and Beguira love him and they are good teachers.

00:13:02.714 --> 00:13:10.158
Baloo likes teaching Mowgli because he is a good student and learns quickly.

00:13:10.218 --> 00:13:17.426
First he teaches him to hunt only when he is hungry and not for fun.

00:13:17.486 --> 00:13:27.678
Then he teaches him to speak to the different jungle people, and he teaches him the important master words.

00:13:27.738 --> 00:13:32.472
Sometimes Mowgli gets tired of these lessons.

00:13:32.531 --> 00:13:38.976
One day he is not listening to his lesson, and Balu gets angry.

00:13:39.036 --> 00:13:47.248
He hits Mowgli gently on the head, and the little boy runs away and climbs a tree.

00:13:47.308 --> 00:13:52.377
Don't hit little Mowgli, says Bagheera.

00:13:52.438 --> 00:13:54.118
He's young.

00:13:54.178 --> 00:13:59.710
How can his little head remember all those long words?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:10.394
Those long words keep him safe from all the birds, snakes and other animals in the jungle.

00:14:10.454 --> 00:14:12.245
Says Baloo.

00:14:12.305 --> 00:14:17.273
I know he's young, but the jungle is big.

00:14:17.333 --> 00:14:20.350
and not always safe.

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:24.602
There are dangers everywhere.

00:14:24.662 --> 00:14:29.056
Then he turns around and calls Mowgli.

00:14:29.116 --> 00:14:35.980
Mowgli, come and say the master words again.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:43.173
Mowgli climbs down the tree and goes to sit with Balu and Vergira.

00:14:43.233 --> 00:14:49.905
I'm going to say the words to Bagheera, not to you, old Baloo.

00:14:49.965 --> 00:14:51.876
Says Moogly.

00:14:51.935 --> 00:14:54.746
I know all the words.

00:14:54.806 --> 00:14:56.437
All right.

00:14:56.497 --> 00:14:58.067
Says Baloo.

00:14:58.127 --> 00:15:04.279
Say the words for the hunting people.

00:15:04.339 --> 00:15:08.950
We are of one blood, you and I.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.591
Says Moogly.

00:15:10.651 --> 00:15:11.959
Good.

00:15:12.019 --> 00:15:17.678
Now say the words for the birds.

00:15:17.738 --> 00:15:19.689
Says balloon.

00:15:19.749 --> 00:15:25.151
Mowgli says the same words but with the sound of a bird.

00:15:25.211 --> 00:15:30.222
And now for the snake people.

00:15:30.282 --> 00:15:32.193
Says balloon.

00:15:32.253 --> 00:15:40.406
Mowgli says the same words but with the long sound of a snake.

00:15:40.466 --> 00:15:42.342
Very good.

00:15:42.402 --> 00:15:44.658
It says Baloo happily.

00:15:44.718 --> 00:15:54.392
With these words, you are safe in the jungle, because no bird, snake or animal can hurt you.

00:15:54.452 --> 00:15:59.664
Now I want to go up in the trees with my people.

00:15:59.724 --> 00:16:02.105
Says Mowgli happily.

00:16:02.165 --> 00:16:03.316
What?

00:16:03.376 --> 00:16:04.986
Says Baloo.

00:16:05.046 --> 00:16:08.418
Do you know the monkey people?

00:16:08.478 --> 00:16:12.903
Suddenly Baloo and Vergira are angry.

00:16:12.963 --> 00:16:16.690
Yes, I know the monkey people.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.462
Says Moogly.

00:16:18.522 --> 00:16:24.046
They take me up in the trees and give me good things to eat.

00:16:24.106 --> 00:16:28.600
They're kind to me and call me brother.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:33.626
They play all day and don't do lessons.

00:16:33.685 --> 00:16:36.368
I like playing with them.

00:16:36.428 --> 00:16:37.999
Oh no.

00:16:38.059 --> 00:16:40.296
Says Baloo angrily.

00:16:40.356 --> 00:16:48.068
You know the law for all of the jungle people, but the monkey people don't have a law.

00:16:48.128 --> 00:16:50.541
They don't have a leader.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.944
They're dirty and noisy.

00:16:54.004 --> 00:16:59.258
They talk all day and forget everything they say.

00:16:59.318 --> 00:17:03.502
The jungle people don't drink where the monkeys drink.

00:17:03.561 --> 00:17:08.094
We don't talk to them or think about them.

00:17:08.154 --> 00:17:11.762
Forget the monkey people, Mowgli.

00:17:11.822 --> 00:17:13.723
Says Baguira.

00:17:13.783 --> 00:17:20.074
They live in the trees and they throw nuts on our heads.

00:17:20.134 --> 00:17:21.564
Oh!

00:17:21.624 --> 00:17:24.185
Says Mowgli sadly.

00:17:24.245 --> 00:17:27.285
I'm very sorry.

00:17:27.345 --> 00:17:37.912
All this time the monkey people are sitting in the trees and they are listening to Baloo, Baguira and Mowgli.

00:17:37.972 --> 00:17:43.839
Suddenly, they throw a lot of nuts and sticks on their heads.

00:17:43.899 --> 00:17:53.753
Baloo and Beguira take Mowgli away to another part of the jungle, and they take a nap.

00:17:53.813 --> 00:18:05.441
Listening Activity First, we are going to find some nuts for breakfast.

00:18:05.501 --> 00:18:12.136
Then you are going to learn all the master words.

00:18:12.196 --> 00:18:22.870
After we are going to get some bananas from the trees and I'm going to find some honey for us to eat.

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:28.021
Bhagira is going to find his own lunch.

00:18:28.081 --> 00:18:34.164
After lunch, Bhagira and I are going to sleep.

00:18:34.224 --> 00:18:42.569
In the afternoon, you are going to hunt with Bagheera.

00:18:42.629 --> 00:18:46.520
CHAPTER IV.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.752
CAR.

00:18:48.812 --> 00:18:56.664
When Baloo and Bagheera wake up after their nap, they can't find Mowgli.

00:18:56.724 --> 00:18:59.366
Where's Mowgli?

00:18:59.426 --> 00:19:01.530
asks Bagheera.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:06.056
Baloo looks up at a tree and sees Mughly.

00:19:06.116 --> 00:19:10.540
The monkey people are holding his legs and arms.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:16.274
Baloo shouts angrily and Bhagira tries to climb up the tree.

00:19:16.334 --> 00:19:20.298
But he is too heavy for the small branches.

00:19:20.358 --> 00:19:25.432
The monkeys laugh loudly and carry Mughly away.

00:19:25.492 --> 00:19:29.998
Baloo and Bhagira are very angry and worried.

00:19:30.058 --> 00:19:36.966
They follow the monkeys and Mowgli, but the monkeys move very quickly.

00:19:37.026 --> 00:19:41.370
It is exciting for Mowgli to fly in the sky.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:48.635
The monkeys jump quickly from tree to tree, but Mowgli is afraid of falling.

00:19:48.696 --> 00:19:51.608
Where are the monkeys taking me?

00:19:51.668 --> 00:19:56.382
He thinks, I must tell Baloo and Bagheera.

00:19:56.442 --> 00:19:58.414
But how?

00:19:58.474 --> 00:20:01.627
Suddenly he sees Ran.

00:20:01.687 --> 00:20:06.769
He is a big bird and he flies high in the blue sky.

00:20:06.829 --> 00:20:10.320
Ran sees the monkeys with a man cub.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:15.452
He flies down and hears the master words of the birds.

00:20:15.512 --> 00:20:19.814
We are of one blood, you and I.

00:20:19.874 --> 00:20:22.906
You speak our language.

00:20:22.966 --> 00:20:24.576
Says Ran.

00:20:24.636 --> 00:20:26.594
Who are you?

00:20:26.654 --> 00:20:29.622
I'm Oakley, the man cup.

00:20:29.683 --> 00:20:31.424
Please help me.

00:20:31.484 --> 00:20:36.656
Find Baloo and Beguira and tell them about the monkeys.

00:20:36.716 --> 00:20:38.137
All right.

00:20:38.197 --> 00:20:39.908
Says Ran.

00:20:39.968 --> 00:20:42.190
I can do that.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.760
And he flies away.

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:52.315
The monkeys move quickly and soon Baloo and Beguira are far behind.

00:20:52.375 --> 00:20:55.940
We're too slow.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.614
says Baloo.

00:20:57.674 --> 00:21:01.006
We can't follow the monkeys.

00:21:01.067 --> 00:21:05.100
Poor Mowgli, he is in danger.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.832
Poor Mowgli, says Bagira.

00:21:08.892 --> 00:21:11.344
Oh, this is terrible.

00:21:11.404 --> 00:21:15.008
His big green eyes are sad.

00:21:15.068 --> 00:21:16.859
I have an idea.

00:21:16.879 --> 00:21:22.504
Where's Carr, the giant python?

00:21:22.565 --> 00:21:26.578
He climbs up trees quickly and easily.

00:21:26.638 --> 00:21:29.510
And he eats monkeys.

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:31.792
Perhaps he can help us.

00:21:31.812 --> 00:21:36.134
Our clever idea, Bhagira.

00:21:36.194 --> 00:21:37.876
Says Baloo.

00:21:37.936 --> 00:21:40.408
Let's look for him.

00:21:40.468 --> 00:21:44.400
They find car lying in the sun.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:48.643
He is a beautiful yellow and brown snake.

00:21:48.703 --> 00:21:51.797
And he is ten metres long.

00:21:51.857 --> 00:21:56.882
He is very strong and very dangerous.

00:21:56.942 --> 00:21:59.374
Hello.

00:21:59.434 --> 00:22:02.695
Says Ka when he sees them.

00:22:02.756 --> 00:22:04.917
Hello Ka.

00:22:04.977 --> 00:22:06.848
Says Baloo.

00:22:06.908 --> 00:22:09.890
We're looking for food.

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:14.613
Oh, I'm very hungry.

00:22:14.673 --> 00:22:16.374
Says Ka.

00:22:16.434 --> 00:22:20.226
Let me come with you.

00:22:20.286 --> 00:22:23.758
We're following the monkey people.

00:22:23.818 --> 00:22:25.638
Says Baloo.

00:22:25.698 --> 00:22:30.950
They have our man cub and we want to find him.

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:35.992
Why are you following the monkey people?

00:22:36.052 --> 00:22:38.214
Ask Scar.

00:22:38.274 --> 00:22:42.665
They took our man cub and we're angry.

00:22:42.725 --> 00:22:44.496
Says Baloo.

00:22:44.556 --> 00:22:48.308
We must find him now.

00:22:48.368 --> 00:22:50.246
Says Bagheera.

00:22:50.306 --> 00:22:57.500
Ka looks interested and says, your man cub?

00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:58.920
Yes.

00:22:58.981 --> 00:23:00.652
Says Baloo.

00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:03.933
Our man cub, Mowgli.

00:23:03.994 --> 00:23:13.950
Beguira is very clever and says, the monkey people always call you bad names.

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:19.483
They say you're an old yellow worm.

00:23:19.544 --> 00:23:23.746
Says car angrily.

00:23:23.807 --> 00:23:32.742
Those noisy, dirty monkeys must not call me bad names.

00:23:32.802 --> 00:23:35.634
Where are they?

00:23:35.694 --> 00:23:40.026
And where is your man cub?

00:23:40.086 --> 00:23:44.059
Suddenly they hear a voice from the sky.

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:46.431
Look up, balloon!

00:23:46.491 --> 00:23:48.496
Shouts ran.

00:23:48.556 --> 00:23:50.510
Hello, Ran.

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:52.302
Shouts, Baloo.

00:23:52.362 --> 00:23:56.375
Mowgli's with the monkey people.

00:23:56.435 --> 00:23:58.106
Cries, Ran.

00:23:58.166 --> 00:24:00.688
He's in the monkey city.

00:24:00.748 --> 00:24:03.261
The lost city.

00:24:03.321 --> 00:24:05.643
Mowgli's clever.

00:24:05.703 --> 00:24:08.616
He knows the master words.

00:24:08.676 --> 00:24:10.927
Good luck.

00:24:10.987 --> 00:24:13.809
The lost city?

00:24:13.870 --> 00:24:15.411
Says Baguira.

00:24:15.471 --> 00:24:16.978
Surprised.

00:24:17.038 --> 00:24:22.266
It's a very old city, and no one lives there.

00:24:22.326 --> 00:24:23.657
Yes.

00:24:23.717 --> 00:24:25.257
Says Baloo.

00:24:25.317 --> 00:24:28.328
Only the monkey people go there.

00:24:28.388 --> 00:24:33.430
We must leave immediately because it's far away.

00:24:33.490 --> 00:24:37.680
You move quickly, but I'm slow.

00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:39.871
I can follow you.

00:24:39.931 --> 00:24:41.302
Yes!

00:24:41.362 --> 00:24:43.642
Let's go!

00:24:43.702 --> 00:24:45.344
says Carr.

00:24:45.404 --> 00:24:48.556
I'm very hungry.

00:24:48.616 --> 00:24:56.733
Those noisy monkeys can't call me an old yellow worm.

00:24:56.753 --> 00:25:04.409
I'm going to teach them something.

00:25:04.469 --> 00:25:09.533
Listening activity.

00:25:09.593 --> 00:25:11.729
One.

00:25:11.789 --> 00:25:14.596
What can you do, Ran?

00:25:14.656 --> 00:25:22.882
I can fly high in the sky and I can sing to everyone below.

00:25:22.942 --> 00:25:25.173
Two.

00:25:25.234 --> 00:25:28.116
What can you do, Beguira?

00:25:28.176 --> 00:25:32.168
I'm a clever and silent hunter.

00:25:32.228 --> 00:25:36.412
I can jump long distances.

00:25:36.472 --> 00:25:38.743
Three.

00:25:38.804 --> 00:25:42.002
What can you do, Kar?

00:25:42.062 --> 00:25:44.952
I can dance.

00:25:45.012 --> 00:25:55.690
All the animals that see me dance want to walk towards me and fall into my mouth.

00:25:55.750 --> 00:26:00.103
Incredible!

00:26:00.163 --> 00:26:09.254
Four, what can you do, Sheerkan?

00:26:09.314 --> 00:26:15.212
Everyone is scared of me.

00:26:15.272 --> 00:26:21.367
Men can't escape me, because I can run very fast.

00:26:21.428 --> 00:26:26.402
And I can swim well too.

00:26:26.462 --> 00:26:32.227
Five, what can you do, Baloo?

00:26:32.287 --> 00:26:41.738
I can speak all the languages of the other animals in the jungle.

00:26:41.798 --> 00:26:53.726
Chapter 5 The Lost City Everything in the Lost City is very old.

00:26:53.786 --> 00:27:01.030
There is a big palace on a hill and a water fountain near the king's garden.

00:27:01.090 --> 00:27:08.360
The houses don't have any roofs and trees are growing inside them.

00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:16.960
The monkey people call this place their city and run around everywhere.

00:27:17.020 --> 00:27:26.534
Some monkeys play with the oranges and flowers in the king's garden and then they fight and shout.

00:27:26.594 --> 00:27:32.626
Others jump up and down and say silly things.

00:27:32.686 --> 00:27:38.053
The monkey people are happy because Mowgli is with them.

00:27:38.113 --> 00:27:42.749
This boy can teach us how to make things.

00:27:42.809 --> 00:27:44.859
Says one monkey.

00:27:44.919 --> 00:27:49.640
Yes, then make things with their hands.

00:27:49.700 --> 00:27:52.100
Says another monkey.

00:27:52.160 --> 00:27:56.682
But monkeys always forget the things they say.

00:27:56.742 --> 00:28:05.352
Mowgli is tired and hungry and says, Bring me some food.

00:28:05.413 --> 00:28:16.501
About 30 noisy monkeys go to get some fruit, but they start fighting and forget to bring the fruit to Mowgli.

00:28:16.561 --> 00:28:21.635
Mowgli doesn't like the monkeys or the lost city.

00:28:21.696 --> 00:28:24.918
Baloo's right, he thinks.

00:28:24.978 --> 00:28:28.202
The monkey people have no law.

00:28:28.262 --> 00:28:30.774
They are different from us.

00:28:30.834 --> 00:28:33.409
I must try to run away.

00:28:33.469 --> 00:28:38.496
Baloo and begira are probably angry with me.

00:28:38.556 --> 00:28:46.309
Mowgli tries to run to the walls of the lost city, but the monkeys pull him back.

00:28:46.369 --> 00:28:49.270
You mustn't go away.

00:28:49.330 --> 00:28:50.922
They shout.

00:28:50.982 --> 00:28:54.063
You're happy here with us.

00:28:54.123 --> 00:28:56.054
We're great.

00:28:56.114 --> 00:28:58.225
We're wonderful.

00:28:58.285 --> 00:29:03.073
We all say this, and it's true.

00:29:03.133 --> 00:29:07.370
Mowgli is tired and confused.

00:29:07.430 --> 00:29:10.330
When do these monkeys sleep?

00:29:10.390 --> 00:29:12.070
He thinks.

00:29:12.130 --> 00:29:18.452
He looks up at the sky and sees a big cloud near the moon.

00:29:18.512 --> 00:29:27.004
Perhaps that cloud is going to hide the moon and I can run away when it's dark.

00:29:27.064 --> 00:29:32.611
Beguira and Ka are also watching the same cloud.

00:29:32.671 --> 00:29:36.738
They are outside the walls of the lost city.

00:29:36.798 --> 00:29:40.090
We must, be careful.

00:29:40.150 --> 00:29:42.071
Says Baguira.

00:29:42.131 --> 00:29:48.564
There are only two of us, and there are hundreds of monkeys.

00:29:48.624 --> 00:29:53.596
They are near the walls, and they're talking to Mowgli.

00:29:53.656 --> 00:30:00.394
When the cloud hides the moon, I'm going to attack them.

00:30:00.454 --> 00:30:02.258
Good idea!

00:30:02.318 --> 00:30:04.190
says Khan.

00:30:04.250 --> 00:30:14.014
I'm going to go up the hill and then I'm going to come down fast!

00:30:14.075 --> 00:30:20.918
Bhagira enters the city walls silently and attacks the monkeys.

00:30:20.978 --> 00:30:25.130
He hits them with his strong black paws.

00:30:25.191 --> 00:30:28.626
The monkeys are scared and scream.

00:30:28.686 --> 00:30:34.072
But one of them shouts, Begearer is alone!

00:30:34.132 --> 00:30:35.413
Kill him!

00:30:35.473 --> 00:30:37.134
Kill him!

00:30:37.194 --> 00:30:44.888
Suddenly, hundreds of monkeys jump on Begearer and hit, kick, and bite him.

00:30:44.948 --> 00:30:49.410
Begearer fights bravely, but he is alone.

00:30:49.471 --> 00:30:54.566
Other monkeys take moogly to an old, broken building.

00:30:54.626 --> 00:31:00.344
They throw him into a dark room with one small window.

00:31:00.404 --> 00:31:07.289
Stay here with the poison people until we kill your friend, Bagira.

00:31:07.350 --> 00:31:09.932
Says one monkey.

00:31:09.992 --> 00:31:13.354
Then we can play.

00:31:13.414 --> 00:31:20.356
In the dark room, Mowgli can hear the hissing sounds of the poison people.

00:31:20.416 --> 00:31:23.144
This room is full of snakes.

00:31:23.204 --> 00:31:27.578
He thinks, I must give the snake's call.

00:31:27.638 --> 00:31:31.842
We are all one blood, you and I.

00:31:31.902 --> 00:31:37.057
He says, giving the snake's call.

00:31:37.117 --> 00:31:41.185
The snake's answer.

00:31:41.245 --> 00:31:45.170
We're not going to bite you.

00:31:45.230 --> 00:31:49.331
But please don't move.

00:31:49.391 --> 00:31:54.322
Because your feet hurt us.

00:31:54.382 --> 00:31:56.182
All right.

00:31:56.242 --> 00:32:01.634
Says Mowgli, listening to the noise of the fight outside.

00:32:01.694 --> 00:32:05.024
But Gira's fighting for his life.

00:32:05.084 --> 00:32:06.715
Thinks Mowgli.

00:32:06.775 --> 00:32:09.064
How can I help him?

00:32:09.124 --> 00:32:14.934
He remembers the big water fountain near the King's Garden.

00:32:14.994 --> 00:32:27.866
He goes to the small window and shouts, Bagheera, go to the water fountain and jump into the water.

00:32:27.926 --> 00:32:37.158
Bagheera hears him and thinks, oh good, Mowgli is safe.

00:32:37.218 --> 00:32:41.528
He slowly goes to the water fountain.

00:32:41.588 --> 00:32:51.382
Finally, Baloo arrives and shouts.

00:32:51.442 --> 00:33:00.104
The monkeys jump on Baloo, and he hits them with his big, strong arms.

00:33:00.164 --> 00:33:08.062
Mowgli hears a loud splash when Bagheera jumps into the water fountain.

00:33:08.123 --> 00:33:14.882
The monkeys are afraid of water and they stand around the fountain.

00:33:14.942 --> 00:33:21.206
Bagheera cannot get out to help balloon.

00:33:21.266 --> 00:33:25.758
Listening activity.

00:33:25.818 --> 00:33:27.300
Hello.

00:33:27.320 --> 00:33:37.644
I'd like some information about your jungle adventure tour to the lost city of Azkhan.

00:33:37.704 --> 00:33:39.363
Oh yes, of course.

00:33:39.423 --> 00:33:41.795
There is a trip every week.

00:33:41.855 --> 00:33:45.508
The next trip leaves on the 10th of July.

00:33:45.568 --> 00:33:47.710
That's next Thursday.

00:33:47.770 --> 00:33:48.950
Good.

00:33:49.010 --> 00:33:51.292
We're here for another week.

00:33:51.352 --> 00:33:53.334
So that's perfect.

00:33:53.394 --> 00:33:56.536
At what time does the tour leave?

00:33:56.596 --> 00:34:00.960
It leaves at half past eight in the morning.

00:34:01.020 --> 00:34:05.804
The mini bus leaves from the tourist information office.

00:34:05.864 --> 00:34:07.730
Do you know where that is?

00:34:07.789 --> 00:34:10.495
Yes, it's in the square.

00:34:10.555 --> 00:34:12.206
Yes, that's right.

00:34:12.266 --> 00:34:15.388
Do you want me to include you in the tour group?

00:34:15.448 --> 00:34:20.711
Yes, it's myself and three other people.

00:34:20.770 --> 00:34:22.942
So there are four of us.

00:34:23.002 --> 00:34:24.402
That's fine.

00:34:24.462 --> 00:34:28.004
I just need one name to make a reservation.

00:34:28.064 --> 00:34:30.386
You can have my name.

00:34:30.446 --> 00:34:33.788
It's Deborah Thompson.

00:34:33.847 --> 00:34:36.229
How do you spell that?

00:34:36.289 --> 00:34:38.337
Deborah is...

00:34:38.397 --> 00:34:47.811
D, E, B, O, R, A, H.

00:34:47.872 --> 00:35:01.802
And Thompson is T, H, O, M, P, S, O, N.

00:35:01.862 --> 00:35:03.794
Thank you, Deborah.

00:35:03.854 --> 00:35:06.977
It's $20 each, right?

00:35:07.037 --> 00:35:08.445
Yes, that's right.

00:35:08.505 --> 00:35:17.409
The price is $20 per person and that includes the bus, lunch at the lost city and a tour guide.

00:35:17.469 --> 00:35:20.932
Thank you.

00:35:20.992 --> 00:35:28.037
Let's meet some of the animals in the story.

00:35:28.097 --> 00:35:31.220
Tigers.

00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:36.194
There are five kinds of tigers in the world.

00:35:36.254 --> 00:35:38.108
The Siberian.

00:35:38.168 --> 00:35:46.614
The Bengal, the Indo-Chinese, the South Chinese and the Sumatran.

00:35:46.674 --> 00:35:53.505
Tigers are big, strong animals and they live in Asia.

00:35:53.566 --> 00:36:01.768
They are carnivorous and they hunt alone at night because they have excellent night vision.

00:36:01.828 --> 00:36:05.598
They are also good swimmers.

00:36:05.658 --> 00:36:11.764
There are only about 7,000 tigers in the world today.

00:36:11.824 --> 00:36:16.868
They are in danger of extinction, and this is very sad.

00:36:16.928 --> 00:36:23.845
People hunt them for their beautiful coats, and this is against the law.

00:36:23.905 --> 00:36:30.686
Many countries are trying to save tigers.

00:36:30.746 --> 00:36:48.116
There are different kinds of bears in the world, the black bear, the grizzly, the Kodiak, the Alaskan brown bear and the polar bear.

00:36:48.176 --> 00:36:54.971
Bears are very big and heavy and have a lot of fur.

00:36:55.032 --> 00:36:59.067
They are strong, lively animals.

00:36:59.127 --> 00:37:11.734
They live in the forests and mountains of North America, Asia and Europe, but polar bears live in the Arctic Circle.

00:37:11.794 --> 00:37:21.328
They are carnivorous animals, but they also like fish, fruit and honey.

00:37:21.388 --> 00:37:30.520
Indian Pythons Indian pythons are from the family of snakes.

00:37:30.580 --> 00:37:37.722
They are very big, long snakes and live in the jungles of India.

00:37:37.782 --> 00:37:41.053
They like living near water.

00:37:41.112 --> 00:37:45.434
They kill animals by squeezing them.

00:37:45.494 --> 00:37:51.259
They don't chew their food, they swallow their prey.

00:37:51.319 --> 00:37:57.714
Indian pythons can even eat big animals like deer.

00:37:57.774 --> 00:38:03.736
After a big meal, they don't eat for days or weeks.

00:38:03.796 --> 00:38:08.118
Pythons are in danger of extinction too.

00:38:08.178 --> 00:38:17.070
People hunt them for their beautiful skin and use it to make bags, shoes and belts.

00:38:17.130 --> 00:38:22.775
In some countries, this is against the law.

00:38:22.835 --> 00:38:26.840
Black Panthers.

00:38:26.900 --> 00:38:31.724
Black Panthers are really black leopards.

00:38:31.784 --> 00:38:36.987
Their coat is very dark, so you can't see its spots.

00:38:37.048 --> 00:38:42.702
Black Panthers live in Asia, Africa and the Far East.

00:38:42.762 --> 00:38:48.326
They are carnivorous and they live in forests and jungles.

00:38:48.386 --> 00:38:52.606
They like climbing up trees and sitting there.

00:38:52.666 --> 00:38:59.136
They are strong, clever animals and they hunt at night.

00:38:59.196 --> 00:39:02.247
Wolves.

00:39:02.307 --> 00:39:05.508
Wolves are social animals.

00:39:05.568 --> 00:39:09.648
They live and hunt together in a pack.

00:39:09.708 --> 00:39:15.380
Each pack has a leader and the other wolves must follow him.

00:39:15.440 --> 00:39:22.500
There are grey, brown, black, red and white wolves.

00:39:22.560 --> 00:39:26.160
They communicate with different sounds.

00:39:26.221 --> 00:39:31.574
They howl, buck and growl.

00:39:31.634 --> 00:39:41.108
Wolves live in the forests and mountains of Alaska, the United States, northern Europe and Russia.

00:39:41.168 --> 00:39:45.100
They are in danger of extinction too.

00:39:45.160 --> 00:39:50.735
There are only about 150,000 wolves in the world today.

00:39:50.795 --> 00:39:57.199
Many of them live in national parks in the United States.

00:39:57.259 --> 00:40:06.331
Many countries have laws that protect wolves.

00:40:06.391 --> 00:40:07.361
6.

00:40:07.421 --> 00:40:19.318
Cars Dance Suddenly, car comes down the hill fast and he is ready to attack the monkeys.

00:40:19.378 --> 00:40:27.408
They all know that Ka can kill any animal and they are afraid of him.

00:40:27.468 --> 00:40:30.870
When they see him, they shout.

00:40:30.930 --> 00:40:32.571
It's Ka!

00:40:32.631 --> 00:40:33.512
Run!

00:40:33.572 --> 00:40:34.782
Run!

00:40:34.842 --> 00:40:42.268
Then Ka opens his mouth and speaks one hissing word.

00:40:42.328 --> 00:40:50.678
The monkeys are suddenly quiet and everything in the lost city is silent.

00:40:50.738 --> 00:40:54.284
Bagheera gets out of the fountain.

00:40:54.344 --> 00:40:57.856
Let's take Mowgli and go.

00:40:57.917 --> 00:40:59.538
He says.

00:40:59.598 --> 00:41:01.938
Thank you, car.

00:41:01.998 --> 00:41:03.330
Yes.

00:41:03.390 --> 00:41:04.920
Thank you, car.

00:41:04.980 --> 00:41:06.591
Says Baloo.

00:41:06.651 --> 00:41:08.962
You're great.

00:41:09.022 --> 00:41:11.434
Look at the monkeys.

00:41:11.494 --> 00:41:14.015
They're terrified.

00:41:14.075 --> 00:41:16.796
I'm happy to help.

00:41:16.856 --> 00:41:18.518
Says car.

00:41:18.578 --> 00:41:22.094
Where's the man cub?

00:41:22.154 --> 00:41:25.060
I'm here with the snakes.

00:41:25.120 --> 00:41:26.950
Crys mowgling.

00:41:27.010 --> 00:41:29.390
I can't get out.

00:41:29.450 --> 00:41:32.071
Take him away.

00:41:32.131 --> 00:41:34.251
Shout the snakes.

00:41:34.311 --> 00:41:41.822
He jumps around and hurts us with his feet.

00:41:41.882 --> 00:41:48.194
The man cub has friends everywhere.

00:41:48.254 --> 00:41:49.996
Says car.

00:41:50.056 --> 00:41:57.354
He hits the wall with his heavy body three times and makes a hole in it.

00:41:57.414 --> 00:42:03.158
Mowgli jumps out and runs to Balu and Beguira.

00:42:03.218 --> 00:42:08.852
Thank you for helping me, says Mowgli, smiling.

00:42:08.913 --> 00:42:12.025
You must thank Ka.

00:42:12.086 --> 00:42:15.078
Say Balu and Beguira.

00:42:15.138 --> 00:42:19.004
Mowgli looks at the Great Python.

00:42:19.064 --> 00:42:25.672
He looks a bit like a monkey, says Carl.

00:42:25.732 --> 00:42:31.066
We're of one blood, you and I, says Moogley.

00:42:31.126 --> 00:42:36.151
I'm your friend, and I can always help you.

00:42:36.211 --> 00:42:45.216
You're brave, and you speak well, says Carl.

00:42:45.276 --> 00:42:52.357
Now you must go with your friends.

00:42:52.417 --> 00:43:04.294
Ka moves softly in front of the sitting monkeys and begins his dance, the hunger dance.

00:43:04.354 --> 00:43:09.196
His head moves slowly from right to left.

00:43:09.257 --> 00:43:21.426
His long body makes circles, squares and other shapes He dances slowly and never stops.

00:43:21.486 --> 00:43:26.928
The monkeys are terrified, but they cannot move.

00:43:26.988 --> 00:43:33.110
Baloo and Beguira look at Carr and cannot move.

00:43:33.170 --> 00:43:37.752
Mowgli cannot understand what is happening.

00:43:37.812 --> 00:43:40.162
Monkeys!

00:43:40.223 --> 00:43:44.954
Cries Carr, can you move?

00:43:45.014 --> 00:43:47.055
No car.

00:43:47.115 --> 00:43:49.266
They answer loudly.

00:43:49.326 --> 00:43:53.947
Without your word, we cannot move.

00:43:54.007 --> 00:43:59.089
Come close to me, monkeys.

00:43:59.149 --> 00:44:03.031
Says car in his low voice.

00:44:03.091 --> 00:44:07.443
Come very close.

00:44:07.503 --> 00:44:16.196
The monkeys move close to Ka, and Baloo and Bagheera move close too.

00:44:16.256 --> 00:44:22.618
Mowgli is worried, and he pulls Baloo and Bagheera away.

00:44:22.678 --> 00:44:25.739
Oh, thank you, Mowgli.

00:44:25.799 --> 00:44:28.170
Wispers, Bagheera.

00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:30.310
What's happening?

00:44:30.370 --> 00:44:32.291
asks Mowgli.

00:44:32.351 --> 00:44:35.052
Your eyes are closing.

00:44:35.112 --> 00:44:37.447
Are you feeling well?

00:44:37.507 --> 00:44:41.454
A python's dance is magic.

00:44:41.514 --> 00:44:44.046
Whisper's baguera.

00:44:44.107 --> 00:44:48.770
It's very dangerous to watch, even for us.

00:44:48.830 --> 00:44:53.903
Because it's easy to walk into his mouth.

00:44:53.963 --> 00:44:57.646
Says Mowgli, surprised.

00:44:57.706 --> 00:45:01.704
The monkeys are moving close to Ka.

00:45:01.764 --> 00:45:10.066
Car is going to have a big dinner tonight with all of those monkeys.

00:45:10.126 --> 00:45:12.638
Wispers Baloo?

00:45:12.698 --> 00:45:17.872
Let's go back to the jungle quickly.

00:45:17.932 --> 00:45:23.806
Baloo, Bagheera and Mowgli leave the lost city.

00:45:23.866 --> 00:45:26.890
They go back to the jungle.

00:45:26.950 --> 00:45:29.802
And now, Mowgli?

00:45:29.862 --> 00:45:31.743
Says Bagheera.

00:45:31.803 --> 00:45:35.465
We must follow the law of the jungle.

00:45:35.525 --> 00:45:40.228
We must punish you for talking to the monkeys.

00:45:40.288 --> 00:45:43.659
You're right, says Mowgli.

00:45:43.719 --> 00:45:46.611
I'm a bad man cub.

00:45:46.671 --> 00:45:50.082
He looks at Baloo sadly.

00:45:50.142 --> 00:45:55.776
We're sorry, but we cannot go against the law of the jungle.

00:45:55.836 --> 00:45:57.606
Says Baloo.

00:45:57.666 --> 00:46:00.324
You must learn, Mowgli.

00:46:00.384 --> 00:46:02.282
says Beguira.

00:46:02.342 --> 00:46:08.276
Beguira hits him softly with his big paw six times.

00:46:08.337 --> 00:46:11.590
But Mowgli does not cry.

00:46:11.650 --> 00:46:14.971
You're a brave man, come.

00:46:15.032 --> 00:46:16.772
Says Baloo.

00:46:16.832 --> 00:46:20.005
Now, Beguira says.

00:46:20.066 --> 00:46:28.170
A jump on my back, little brother, and always remember to follow the law of the jungle.

00:46:28.230 --> 00:46:32.161
It's a good law, and it keeps you safe.

00:46:32.222 --> 00:46:34.282
Let's go home.

00:46:34.342 --> 00:46:37.284
Yes, says Mowgli.

00:46:37.344 --> 00:46:39.724
I want to go home.

00:46:39.784 --> 00:46:46.168
He soon falls asleep on Begearer's back.

00:46:46.228 --> 00:47:00.990
Chapter 7 The Red Flower All of the jungle people are Mowgli's friends, but not Sheer Khan.

00:47:01.051 --> 00:47:04.082
Beguira tells Mowgli.

00:47:04.142 --> 00:47:07.064
Be careful of Sheer Khan.

00:47:07.124 --> 00:47:09.295
He wants to kill you.

00:47:09.356 --> 00:47:13.618
A Kayla likes you, but he's old now.

00:47:13.678 --> 00:47:15.839
He's not strong.

00:47:15.899 --> 00:47:19.070
The young wolves don't listen to him.

00:47:19.130 --> 00:47:22.152
They listen to Sheer Khan.

00:47:22.212 --> 00:47:26.404
One day, you must kill him.

00:47:26.464 --> 00:47:31.275
I'm not afraid, says Mowgli laughing.

00:47:31.336 --> 00:47:34.266
I have you and Balu.

00:47:34.326 --> 00:47:38.388
Mowgli, you must listen to me.

00:47:38.448 --> 00:47:41.428
Says Baguira softly.

00:47:41.488 --> 00:47:46.890
Remember, you're a man cub, not a wolf cub.

00:47:46.950 --> 00:47:50.621
You belong to the world of men.

00:47:50.682 --> 00:47:52.819
They're your brothers.

00:47:52.879 --> 00:47:57.238
One day, you must return to that world.

00:47:57.298 --> 00:48:02.582
You're clever, and you can do a lot of things we can't do.

00:48:02.642 --> 00:48:05.054
Because you're a man.

00:48:05.114 --> 00:48:07.285
Yes, Mowgli.

00:48:07.345 --> 00:48:09.006
Says Baloo.

00:48:09.066 --> 00:48:12.488
Sheer Khan's making trouble for you.

00:48:12.549 --> 00:48:16.240
The young wolves want to kill you.

00:48:16.300 --> 00:48:18.052
But why?

00:48:18.112 --> 00:48:19.863
Asks Mowgli.

00:48:19.923 --> 00:48:21.494
Look at me.

00:48:21.554 --> 00:48:23.920
Says Bagheera.

00:48:23.980 --> 00:48:31.308
Mowgli looks him in the eyes, but Beguira turns his head away quickly.

00:48:31.368 --> 00:48:33.059
That's why.

00:48:33.119 --> 00:48:34.590
He says.

00:48:34.650 --> 00:48:39.222
You see, Mowgli, even I can't look into your eyes.

00:48:39.282 --> 00:48:40.983
You're a man.

00:48:41.043 --> 00:48:42.724
You're clever.

00:48:42.784 --> 00:48:47.416
The young wolves know this, and they hate you.

00:48:47.476 --> 00:48:52.772
Mowgli listens to Beguira and Balu quietly.

00:48:52.832 --> 00:48:58.428
You must go to the men's village and take some of their red flower.

00:48:58.488 --> 00:49:00.580
Says Bagira.

00:49:00.640 --> 00:49:04.432
All of the animals are afraid of it.

00:49:04.493 --> 00:49:09.736
It's a strong friend and it can help you.

00:49:09.796 --> 00:49:17.682
The red flower is fire, but the animals do not call it by its name.

00:49:17.743 --> 00:49:21.181
Very well, says Moogly.

00:49:21.241 --> 00:49:27.258
I'm going to the men's village to get the red flower now.

00:49:27.318 --> 00:49:34.900
In the village, he sees a young boy cover a fire pot with a cloth.

00:49:34.960 --> 00:49:41.552
Mowgli takes the pot from the boy and runs back to the jungle.

00:49:41.612 --> 00:49:55.018
That evening, the jackal to backwee goes to see Mowgli and says, There's a meeting at Council Rock tomorrow morning.

00:49:55.078 --> 00:50:03.701
When Mowgli gets to Council Rock, Akela is not sitting on top of the big rock.

00:50:03.761 --> 00:50:07.252
He is sitting next to it.

00:50:07.312 --> 00:50:15.290
Sheer Khan is there too, and all of the young wolves are sitting around him.

00:50:15.350 --> 00:50:22.520
Mowgli sits next to Bagheera with the firepot between his legs.

00:50:22.580 --> 00:50:28.792
Sheer Khan starts speaking, and Mowgli jumps up.

00:50:28.852 --> 00:50:32.224
Is Sheer Khan your leader?

00:50:32.284 --> 00:50:34.275
asks Mowgli.

00:50:34.335 --> 00:50:37.726
Does he belong to the wolf pack?

00:50:37.786 --> 00:50:41.488
Akhala's old now.

00:50:41.548 --> 00:50:44.110
He's not important.

00:50:44.170 --> 00:50:46.476
Says Sheer Khan.

00:50:46.536 --> 00:50:49.062
Listen to me.

00:50:49.122 --> 00:50:54.216
A man cub doesn't belong to a wolf pack.

00:50:54.276 --> 00:50:57.438
Give him to me.

00:50:57.498 --> 00:50:59.278
A man!

00:50:59.338 --> 00:51:02.490
Cry the young wolves.

00:51:02.530 --> 00:51:06.152
A man doesn't belong to our wolf pack.

00:51:06.212 --> 00:51:12.646
Akhila is angry and says, Mowgli's our brother.

00:51:12.706 --> 00:51:16.342
He respects the law of the jungle.

00:51:16.402 --> 00:51:20.368
Let him go away safely.

00:51:20.428 --> 00:51:21.329
But he's a man.

00:51:21.349 --> 00:51:21.649
But he's a man.

00:51:21.689 --> 00:51:21.989
But he's a man.

00:51:22.009 --> 00:51:22.710
But he's a man.

00:51:22.770 --> 00:51:25.252
But he's a man.

00:51:25.312 --> 00:51:25.872
But he's a man.

00:51:25.913 --> 00:51:28.775
But he's a man.

00:51:28.795 --> 00:51:30.056
But he's a man.

00:51:30.116 --> 00:51:32.338
But he's a man.

00:51:32.358 --> 00:51:33.099
But he's a man.

00:51:33.159 --> 00:51:33.929
But he's a man.

00:51:33.989 --> 00:51:39.530
But he's a man.

00:51:39.590 --> 00:51:51.174
The wolves and the tiger are afraid of the fire and move away from Mowgli.

00:51:51.234 --> 00:51:56.108
You're the leader now, says Bagira.

00:51:56.168 --> 00:51:59.370
Help your friend Akayla.

00:51:59.430 --> 00:52:04.154
I want to go to my people, says Mowgli.

00:52:04.214 --> 00:52:13.928
But first, he goes to Sheer Khan and says, you want to kill me.

00:52:13.988 --> 00:52:17.506
But now you're afraid of me."

00:52:17.566 --> 00:52:25.128
He hits Sheer Khan on the head with his burning stick and burns it a bit.

00:52:25.188 --> 00:52:28.468
The tiger is terrified.

00:52:28.529 --> 00:52:32.370
Go away now, says Mowgli.

00:52:32.430 --> 00:52:42.894
But remember, I'm going to kill you one day, and you must not kill my friend, Akayla.

00:52:42.954 --> 00:52:47.568
He is free to live in the jungle.

00:52:47.628 --> 00:52:53.439
Mowgli jumps at the young wolves with his burning stick.

00:52:53.499 --> 00:52:58.741
They are terrified and run away with Sheer Khan.

00:52:58.801 --> 00:53:06.984
Only Akayla, Beguira and some old wolves stay at Council Rock.

00:53:07.044 --> 00:53:12.518
Suddenly, something inside Mowgli hurts.

00:53:12.578 --> 00:53:15.822
And he starts crying.

00:53:15.882 --> 00:53:19.164
What's happening to me?

00:53:19.224 --> 00:53:21.575
He asks Bagheera.

00:53:21.635 --> 00:53:24.065
Am I dying?

00:53:24.126 --> 00:53:26.236
You're a man.

00:53:26.296 --> 00:53:29.697
And these are tears.

00:53:29.758 --> 00:53:32.098
Says Bagheera.

00:53:32.158 --> 00:53:34.909
They're only tears.

00:53:34.969 --> 00:53:38.214
Now you must go to your people.

00:53:38.274 --> 00:53:44.260
You can't stay in the jungle anymore, my little brother.

00:53:44.320 --> 00:53:51.002
Yes, I must go to the world of men, says Mowgli.

00:53:51.062 --> 00:53:56.994
But first, I want to say goodbye to my mother and father.

00:53:57.054 --> 00:54:03.939
He goes to the cave and cries on his mother's coat.

00:54:03.999 --> 00:54:07.903
Please don't forget me.

00:54:07.963 --> 00:54:11.534
Says Mowgli, crying.

00:54:11.594 --> 00:54:13.605
Forget you.

00:54:13.666 --> 00:54:16.046
Says Mother Wolf.

00:54:16.106 --> 00:54:17.858
Never.

00:54:17.918 --> 00:54:20.328
We love you.

00:54:20.388 --> 00:54:23.210
Come and visit us often.

00:54:23.270 --> 00:54:25.912
Says Father Wolf.

00:54:25.972 --> 00:54:29.688
Your mother and I are getting old.

00:54:29.748 --> 00:54:35.943
When I come to visit, I'm going to bring Sheer Khan's coat.

00:54:36.003 --> 00:54:38.224
Says Mowgli.

00:54:38.284 --> 00:54:46.574
The next morning, he goes down the hill to the world of men.

00:54:46.634 --> 00:54:53.606
Chapter 8 Tiger, Tiger.

00:54:53.666 --> 00:54:57.277
I have a lot of enemies now.

00:54:57.337 --> 00:54:59.224
Mowgli thinks.

00:54:59.284 --> 00:55:01.960
I must go far away."

00:55:02.020 --> 00:55:10.323
He runs and runs until he comes to a village near a lot of rocks and ravines.

00:55:10.383 --> 00:55:15.414
He sees cows and buffaloes everywhere.

00:55:15.475 --> 00:55:19.446
Some boys are looking after them.

00:55:19.506 --> 00:55:23.982
When they see mowgli, they run away.

00:55:24.042 --> 00:55:28.849
Men here are afraid of the people of the jungle.

00:55:28.909 --> 00:55:31.420
Thanks, Mowgli.

00:55:31.480 --> 00:55:35.810
Mowgli sits near the village gate.

00:55:35.870 --> 00:55:42.932
When he sees a man, he opens his mouth to show that he wants some food.

00:55:42.993 --> 00:55:49.214
The man is surprised and runs to the village shouting.

00:55:49.274 --> 00:55:54.188
He comes back with about a hundred people.

00:55:54.248 --> 00:55:57.772
Everyone looks at Mowgli.

00:55:57.832 --> 00:56:04.176
Look, he has the bite marks of wolves on his arms and legs.

00:56:04.236 --> 00:56:06.328
Says one man.

00:56:06.388 --> 00:56:08.410
He's a wolf-choiled.

00:56:08.470 --> 00:56:11.142
He comes from the jungle.

00:56:11.202 --> 00:56:14.634
These men don't understand.

00:56:14.694 --> 00:56:16.586
Think, Mowgli.

00:56:16.646 --> 00:56:19.458
I don't have bite marks.

00:56:19.518 --> 00:56:22.096
I have play marks.

00:56:22.156 --> 00:56:27.662
Wolf cubs always bite lightly when they play.

00:56:27.722 --> 00:56:33.344
He's a good looking boy, says one woman.

00:56:33.404 --> 00:56:35.924
But he's thin.

00:56:35.984 --> 00:56:44.026
He must eat poor boy, says Masua, another woman.

00:56:44.086 --> 00:56:48.110
He can come home with me.

00:56:48.170 --> 00:56:55.556
Missua takes Mowgli to her house and gives him some bread and milk.

00:56:55.616 --> 00:56:58.798
She is kind to him.

00:56:58.858 --> 00:57:05.300
This is my first time in a house, and I don't like it.

00:57:05.360 --> 00:57:07.171
Thanks Mowgli.

00:57:07.231 --> 00:57:12.880
But I'm a man now, and I must do what men do.

00:57:12.940 --> 00:57:20.970
I know the languages of the jungle, and now I must learn the language of men."

00:57:21.031 --> 00:57:33.318
That day, Mowgli learns a lot of words from Masua, but at night he does not want to sleep inside a house.

00:57:33.378 --> 00:57:42.218
He climbs out of a small window and goes to sleep under a big tree near the village.

00:57:42.278 --> 00:57:47.297
He meets Gray Brother, a wolf cub.

00:57:47.357 --> 00:57:50.239
Hello, little brother.

00:57:50.300 --> 00:57:52.621
Says Gray Brother.

00:57:52.681 --> 00:57:55.342
I have news for you.

00:57:55.402 --> 00:57:58.706
Sheer Khan's in the mountains now.

00:57:58.766 --> 00:58:03.008
But he wants to kill you when he comes back.

00:58:03.069 --> 00:58:09.253
Please come to the big tree and tell me when Sheer Khan comes back.

00:58:09.313 --> 00:58:11.285
Says Moogly.

00:58:11.345 --> 00:58:13.737
Yes, little brother.

00:58:13.797 --> 00:58:16.338
Says grey brother.

00:58:16.399 --> 00:58:20.030
And don't forget your wolf family.

00:58:20.091 --> 00:58:24.204
I can't forget the family I love.

00:58:24.264 --> 00:58:27.266
Says Mowgli smiling.

00:58:27.326 --> 00:58:32.048
For three months Mowgli lives in the village.

00:58:32.108 --> 00:58:37.982
He learns to wear clothes, use money and work.

00:58:38.042 --> 00:58:43.514
Every day He looks after cows and buffaloes.

00:58:43.574 --> 00:58:50.186
One day, Mowgli sees Grey Brother at the big tree.

00:58:50.246 --> 00:58:53.238
Sheer Khan is back.

00:58:53.298 --> 00:58:55.478
Says Grey Brother.

00:58:55.538 --> 00:59:00.030
He wants to meet you outside the village gate tonight.

00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:04.411
But now he's hiding in the big ravine.

00:59:04.472 --> 00:59:06.762
Thank you, Grey Brother.

00:59:06.822 --> 00:59:08.568
Says Mowgli.

00:59:08.629 --> 00:59:11.085
He thinks for a moment.

00:59:11.145 --> 00:59:17.640
Then he looks at Gray Brother and says, The big ravine.

00:59:17.700 --> 00:59:24.904
I can take the buffaloes to the top and run after Sheer Khan down the ravine.

00:59:24.964 --> 00:59:29.366
The cows can stay at the bottom of the ravine.

00:59:29.426 --> 00:59:36.675
In this way, he is between the buffaloes and the cows and he can't run away.

00:59:36.735 --> 00:59:41.522
You're right, says Gray Brother excitedly.

00:59:41.582 --> 00:59:43.584
Can you help me?

00:59:43.644 --> 00:59:45.645
Ask Smogley.

00:59:45.706 --> 00:59:48.578
A tailor and I can help you.

00:59:48.638 --> 00:59:54.272
Says Gray Brother, and a tailor comes out from the trees.

00:59:54.332 --> 00:59:58.235
A tailor, cries Smogley happily.

00:59:58.295 --> 01:00:00.868
You're a true friend.

01:00:00.928 --> 01:00:05.901
Take the cows to the bottom of the ravine, grey brother.

01:00:05.961 --> 01:00:07.752
Says Mowgli.

01:00:07.812 --> 01:00:14.306
At Kayla and I are going to take the buffaloes to the top.

01:00:14.366 --> 01:00:18.317
When Mowgli is ready, he shouts.

01:00:18.377 --> 01:00:20.178
Sheer Khan!

01:00:20.238 --> 01:00:21.588
It's me!

01:00:21.648 --> 01:00:23.120
Mowgli!

01:00:23.180 --> 01:00:25.451
Are you ready?

01:00:25.511 --> 01:00:35.070
Mowgli gets on Rama, one of the buffaloes, and they all start running down the ravine.

01:00:35.130 --> 01:00:42.516
Sheer Khan is sleeping, and he wakes up slowly when he hears the noise.

01:00:42.576 --> 01:00:46.300
The buffaloes are running towards him.

01:00:46.360 --> 01:00:52.695
He starts running down the ravine, but he is heavy with food.

01:00:52.755 --> 01:00:57.228
At the bottom of the ravine, he meets the cows.

01:00:57.288 --> 01:01:03.732
He falls under the feet of the buffaloes and they run over him.

01:01:03.792 --> 01:01:13.328
Mowgli jumps off Rama's back, runs towards the tiger and shouts, Sheer Khan's dead!

01:01:13.388 --> 01:01:15.619
He's dead!

01:01:15.679 --> 01:01:22.944
He takes his knife and starts cutting the coat from Sheer Khan's body.

01:01:23.004 --> 01:01:25.896
It is hard work.

01:01:25.956 --> 01:01:34.270
The village hunter, Baldeo, sees Sheer Khan's coat and thinks.

01:01:34.290 --> 01:01:36.851
I want that tiger coat.

01:01:36.911 --> 01:01:40.342
He goes to talk to Mowgli.

01:01:40.402 --> 01:01:44.024
Go and look after your cows.

01:01:44.084 --> 01:01:45.384
He says.

01:01:45.444 --> 01:01:48.676
The tiger coat is mine.

01:01:48.736 --> 01:01:50.986
I'm the village hunter.

01:01:51.046 --> 01:01:54.778
I can sell it for a lot of money.

01:01:54.838 --> 01:01:55.998
No!

01:01:56.058 --> 01:01:57.760
Cries Mowgli.

01:01:57.820 --> 01:02:00.422
Don't touch this coat.

01:02:00.482 --> 01:02:02.104
Listen, boy.

01:02:02.164 --> 01:02:04.186
Says Baldeio.

01:02:04.246 --> 01:02:13.874
Suddenly, a Kayla jumps on him, and he is on the ground with a big grey wolf on top of him.

01:02:13.934 --> 01:02:17.987
Now, go back to the village, Baldeio.

01:02:18.047 --> 01:02:20.250
Says Mowgli.

01:02:20.310 --> 01:02:24.912
Baldeo is afraid and goes away.

01:02:24.972 --> 01:02:32.064
That evening, Mowgli goes back to the village and sees the people at the gate.

01:02:32.124 --> 01:02:34.775
Go away Wolf child!

01:02:34.836 --> 01:02:36.426
Jungle boy!

01:02:36.486 --> 01:02:38.146
They shout.

01:02:38.206 --> 01:02:41.508
We don't want you here!

01:02:41.568 --> 01:02:45.159
They start throwing stones at him.

01:02:45.219 --> 01:02:48.358
Mowgli doesn't understand.

01:02:48.418 --> 01:02:53.790
Sheer Khan kills their cows and takes their children.

01:02:53.850 --> 01:02:59.612
He thinks, but the people of the village are angry with me.

01:02:59.672 --> 01:03:04.184
They're like the bad young wolves of the pack.

01:03:04.245 --> 01:03:15.160
He looks at the stars in the night sky and says, I don't want to sleep in houses anymore.

01:03:15.220 --> 01:03:23.621
He turns to a cayler and says, Let's take Sheer Khan's coat and go away.

01:03:23.682 --> 01:03:29.364
Mowgli and the two wolves go to Mother Wolf's cave.

01:03:29.424 --> 01:03:33.335
The people of the village don't want me, Mother.

01:03:33.395 --> 01:03:35.255
Says Mowgli.

01:03:35.316 --> 01:03:37.616
This is my home.

01:03:37.676 --> 01:03:40.648
I want to stay here.

01:03:40.708 --> 01:03:45.089
And this is Sheer Khan's coat.

01:03:45.149 --> 01:03:48.752
Mother Wolf is very happy.

01:03:48.812 --> 01:03:56.826
Bagheera comes to the cave and says, We're happy to see you, little brother.

01:03:56.886 --> 01:04:03.688
Mowgli takes Sheer Khan's coat and puts it on Council Rock.

01:04:03.748 --> 01:04:10.651
A Kayla sits on it and says, Look carefully, wolves.

01:04:10.711 --> 01:04:14.797
Sheer Khan is dead.

01:04:14.857 --> 01:04:20.897
Now I don't belong to the wolf pack or to the man pack.

01:04:20.957 --> 01:04:22.448
Says Mowgliem.

01:04:22.508 --> 01:04:26.152
But I can hunt alone in the jungle.

01:04:26.212 --> 01:04:28.964
We can hunt with you.

01:04:29.024 --> 01:04:33.408
Say grey brother and the other cubs.

01:04:33.468 --> 01:04:40.315
Mowgli returns to the jungle and lives and hunts with his brothers.

